    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "va-community-care",
    "sort_order": 3,
    "quick_answer": "Yes. Under VA's best medical interest rule, an unusual or excessive travel burden can qualify you for Community Care. That includes long or hard drives, water or terrain barriers, bad weather or traffic, a medical condition that makes travel difficult, a compelling reason, or needing someone to help you travel. You and your VA clinician decide together.",
