    "quick_answer": "Getting Medicare before 65 doesn't end CHAMPVA. But if you're entitled to Medicare Part A, you must also enroll in Part B to keep CHAMPVA. If you cancel Part B, CHAMPVA ends the same day. Medicare Advantage counts. Then Medicare pays first and CHAMPVA second. Send VA your Medicare card and Form 10-7959c.",
