    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "champva",
    "sort_order": 5,
    "quick_answer": "Yes. If VA decided the Veteran died from a service-connected condition, the surviving spouse can qualify for CHAMPVA. The Veteran didn't need a permanent and total rating. Remarrying before age 55 ends CHAMPVA, but remarrying at 55 or older doesn't, and eligibility can come back if a pre-55 remarriage ends.",
