    "quick_answer": "CHAMPVA covers genetic testing and genetic counseling when they're medically necessary, like testing to diagnose a disease or syndrome, BRCA testing for high-risk women, or chromosome testing for infertility or repeated miscarriage. It doesn't cover routine or on-demand genetic tests, paternity tests, or tests to learn a baby's sex. A doctor's order alone isn't enough.",
