    "category_slug": "champva",
    "sort_order": 2,
    "quick_answer": "CHAMPVA covers medically necessary mental health care, including therapy, psychiatric visits, testing, medication management, intensive outpatient programs, partial hospitalization, residential treatment, and inpatient care. Routine outpatient therapy doesn't need approval. Higher levels of care do, unless your other insurance approved them or it's an emergency. The old visit limits were removed in 2024.",
