    "published_at": "2026-09-19T18:06:20.701+00:00",
    "public_updated_at": "2026-10-14T18:39:50.710781+00:00",
    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "champva",
    "sort_order": 4,
    "quick_answer": "Yes. If VA had rated the Veteran permanently and totally disabled from a service-connected condition when they died, a surviving spouse or child can qualify for CHAMPVA, even if the death itself wasn't service connected. The usual CHAMPVA rules still apply, including the TRICARE rule and, for spouses, the remarriage rules.",
