    "quick_answer": "Choosing Chapter 35 education benefits (DEA) after 18 affects whether VA pays the Veteran extra compensation for that child. CHAMPVA is a separate benefit with its own test: an unmarried child 18 to 23 who's enrolled in school. Keep the school certification on file with CHAMPVA, and confirm the child's status with CHAMPVA directly if anything changes.",
