    "sort_order": 3,
    "quick_answer": "Community Care eligibility decisions are appealed through VA's clinical appeals process, not the Board of Veterans' Appeals. Get the decision in writing, then send a written appeal with your evidence to your facility's Patient Advocate. The facility chief medical officer decides, and you can appeal to your regional VISN office.",
    "in_practice_markdown": "Before you file a clinical appeal, make sure you have VA's decision in writing. Many of the denials people bring to us were only said out loud on a phone call. A polite Secure Message that points to the regulation and asks VA to confirm its position in writing usually gets the referral approved. If it doesn't, you'll have a written denial to appeal. Steps and a ready-to-send message: [What to do if your Community Care referral is delayed or stuck](/resources/va-community-care/referral-delays-patient-advocate).",
