    "quick_answer": "Mental health Community Care denials are appealed through VA's clinical appeals process, not the Board of Veterans' Appeals. First, get the decision and reason in writing. Then send a written appeal with supporting records to your facility's Patient Advocate. The facility's chief medical officer decides, and you can appeal to your VISN.",
    "in_practice_markdown": "Most mental health referral refusals we hear about happen on the phone, often with the claim that the 20-day standard only applies to new patients. Before starting a formal appeal, get VA's position in writing: a short Secure Message that points to 38 CFR 17.4040(a) and asks VA to confirm its answer. In our experience, that resolves it most of the time. If it doesn't, the written reply is exactly what your appeal needs. Steps and a ready-to-send message: [What to do if your Community Care referral is delayed or stuck](/resources/va-community-care/referral-delays-patient-advocate).",
