    "status": "published",
    "published_at": "2026-10-14T18:39:50.710781+00:00",
    "public_updated_at": "2026-10-14T18:39:50.710781+00:00",
    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "champva",
    "sort_order": 1,
    "quick_answer": "Start with providers who take Medicare or TRICARE, then call and ask, \"Do you bill CHAMPVA, payer ID 84146?\" If the front desk isn't sure, ask them to check with billing. CHAMPVA doesn't have a network, so any licensed provider who agrees to bill it can treat you.",
    "in_practice_markdown": "The most common reason people think a provider doesn't take CHAMPVA is that they asked the wrong question.\n\nMost insurance runs on networks, so the people who check coverage at a provider's office are trained to look up which plans the office is in network with. CHAMPVA isn't a network plan, so it won't show up on that list. That's when you hear \"we don't take CHAMPVA,\" even from offices that do bill it.\n\nYou just have to ask the right question, the right way. Don't ask whether they're in network with CHAMPVA. Ask whether they bill to payer ID 84146, and if the person on the phone isn't sure, ask them to check with billing. We see that one question turn a lot of \"no\"s into \"yes\"es.\n\nA good starting point: if an office takes Medicare and TRICARE, it's very likely already set up to take CHAMPVA.",
    "reviewed_by": "ValorWell",
