    "sort_order": 1,
    "quick_answer": "CHAMPVA has no network, so any licensed therapist, counselor, social worker, psychologist, or psychiatrist can see you if they're willing to bill CHAMPVA. Ask whether they bill payer ID 84146 and accept assignment. Routine outpatient therapy doesn't need a referral. After your deductible, you usually pay 25% of CHAMPVA's allowable amount per session.",
    "in_practice_markdown": "The most common reason people think a therapist doesn't take CHAMPVA is that they asked the wrong question. The people who check coverage at a therapy office are usually trained to look up which insurance networks the practice belongs to. CHAMPVA isn't a network plan, so it won't be on that list, and you'll hear \"we don't take CHAMPVA\" even from practices that do bill it.\n\nAsk whether they bill to payer ID 84146, and if the person you're talking to isn't sure, ask them to check with billing. A good starting point: practices that take Medicare and TRICARE are very likely already set up to take CHAMPVA.",
