    "quick_answer": "Ask your VA care team for the care you need and say you'd like Community Care. They check your eligibility, confirm your choice, and prepare a referral, which VA says can take up to 14 days. Then you or VA schedule it. Don't go to a routine appointment until VA has approved the care.",
    "in_practice_markdown": "If you ask for a referral and get a \"no\" on the phone, don't stop there. In our experience, the fastest fix is putting the same request in writing through Secure Messaging, pointing to the exact access-standard regulation, and asking VA to confirm its answer in writing. That usually gets the referral submitted. Steps and a ready-to-send message: [What to do if your Community Care referral is delayed or stuck](/resources/va-community-care/referral-delays-patient-advocate).",
