    "slug": "refill-renew-meds-by-mail-prescription",
    "title": "How to Refill or Renew a CHAMPVA Meds by Mail Prescription",
    "primary_question": "How do I refill or renew an existing CHAMPVA Meds by Mail prescription, how long can it take, and what should I do to avoid running out of medication?",
    "summary": "Refill CHAMPVA Meds by Mail prescriptions online, by phone, or by mail. Here's how long each takes and what to do when you're out of refills.",
    "body_markdown": "## Refill or renewal?\n\n- **Refill:** the prescription is active and has refills left. Use any of the three methods below.\n- **Renewal:** the prescription expired or has no refills. Call Meds by Mail and ask for a renewal.\n\nTrying the refill line over and over won't fix an expired prescription.\n\nNever used Meds by Mail for this drug? See [How to start a new Meds by Mail prescription](/resources/champva/start-meds-by-mail-prescription).\n\n## Three ways to refill\n\n| Method | How | Time to arrive |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Online | VA's [prescription tool](https://www.va.gov/health-care/manage-prescriptions-medications/) | Up to 10 days |\n| Phone | Automated line, 888-370-1699, 24/7 | Up to 10 days |\n| Mail | Bar-coded refill slip to Meds by Mail, PO Box 331178, Murfreesboro, TN 37133 | Up to 15 days |\n\nTimes come from VA's [Meds by Mail page](https://www.va.gov/resources/meds-by-mail-for-champva-and-other-family-member-programs/).\n\nFor the phone line, have your **full Social Security number** and **prescription number** ready. Only give your Social Security number on a call you made to the official number.\n\nFor mail, VA suggests sending the refill slip **as soon as each delivery arrives**. Mail is the slowest option.\n\nOnline, you can also track shipments.\n\n## How to renew\n\nCall the Meds by Mail Service Center at 866-229-7389 or 888-385-0235, Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 7:30 p.m. Eastern. Ask for a prescription renewal.\n\nRenewals can take longer than refills, so start when you see you're on your last refill, not when you're on your last pills.\n\n## How to avoid running out\n\n1. Check refills left and the expiration date each time a shipment arrives.\n2. Use online or phone when timing is tight.\n3. Mail the refill slip right away if you use mail.\n4. Track shipments online.\n5. Don't rely on Meds by Mail for something urgent.\n\nIf you're about to run out, ask your prescriber for a short-term supply to fill at an OptumRx network pharmacy. That's covered under the regular pharmacy rules. More here: [CHAMPVA prescription coverage](/resources/champva/prescription-drug-coverage).\n\n## If a refill doesn't go through\n\nCheck:\n\n- Are there refills left?\n- Has it expired?\n- Is the prescription number right?\n- Did you get other drug coverage? That ends Meds by Mail eligibility.\n- Is the drug still available through Meds by Mail?\n\nIf it's still unclear, call the Service Center instead of resubmitting.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "answer": "Up to 10 days online or by phone, up to 15 by mail.",
        "question": "How long does a Meds by Mail refill take?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "888-370-1699, available 24/7.",
        "question": "What's the Meds by Mail refill number?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Call Meds by Mail at 866-229-7389 or 888-385-0235 and ask for a renewal.",
        "question": "My prescription has no refills left. What do I do?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, through VA's prescription tool.",
        "question": "Can I refill online?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Ask your prescriber for a short-term supply at an OptumRx network pharmacy.",
        "question": "I'm almost out. What now?"
      }
    ],
