    "slug": "military-health-benefits",
    "title": "Military Health Benefits Resources",
    "primary_question": "What should military families understand about navigating TRICARE and other military health coverage questions?",
    "summary": "Practical resources for military families navigating TRICARE, coordination of benefits, coverage questions, and other military health-benefit issues.",
    "body_markdown": "## About this category\n\nMilitary health-benefit questions can become confusing quickly because eligibility, enrollment, referrals, authorizations, networks, claims, and coordination with other insurance are separate issues. Resources in this category are designed to explain those moving parts in plain language and help military families identify what to verify with the appropriate official program.\n\n## Use this category for\n\n- Understanding how TRICARE interacts with other health insurance\n- Separating eligibility questions from claims and coordination-of-benefits questions\n- Preparing better questions before contacting TRICARE, a provider, or another insurer\n- Understanding common administrative terms and processes that affect access or payment\n- Identifying when program-specific guidance should be verified directly with the official health-benefit program\n\n## Verify current program rules\n\nMilitary health-benefit rules can vary by beneficiary category, plan, service status, location, and type of coverage. These resources are educational and should not replace current guidance from TRICARE, the Defense Health Agency, another applicable program, or a beneficiary's health plan.\n\n*Last researched: September 16, 2026.*",
