    "primary_question": "What opportunities are there for licensed therapists to serve veterans and military families by telehealth in Maine?",
    "summary": "ValorWell needs licensed therapists in Maine to treat Veterans and their families by telehealth. Licenses, compacts, VA care, and how it works.",
    "body_markdown": "## Is ValorWell hiring therapists in Maine?\n\nYes. ValorWell has a great need for more licensed therapists in Maine. Veterans, Veteran spouses, and children of Veterans there are looking for therapists who accept CHAMPVA and VA Community Care, and there aren't enough.\n\nVA estimates about 102,362 Veterans live in Maine, according to VA's [fiscal year 2025 Annual Benefits Report](https://benefits.va.gov/REPORTS/abr/docs/2025-abr.pdf).\n\n## Which licenses can treat Veterans and families in Maine?\n\nThe independent counselor license in Maine is the **LCPC** (Licensed Clinical Professional Counselor), issued by the [Maine Board of Counseling Professionals Licensure](https://www.maine.gov/pfr/professionallicensing/professions/board-of-counseling-professionals-licensure/licensing-and-forms). Licensed marriage and family therapists, independently licensed clinical social workers, and licensed psychologists in Maine also qualify, under the titles Maine uses.\n\nFor telehealth, the license has to match where the client is sitting during the session. To see a client located in Maine, you need a Maine license or a valid compact privilege. See [Can Therapists See Telehealth Clients in Another State?](/resources/for-therapists/telehealth-licensure-client-location)\n\n## Can you practice in Maine through a compact?\n\n- **Counseling Compact:** Maine has enacted the compact but wasn't yet listed as issuing privileges as of October 2026. Until it does, counselors need a Maine license.\n- **PSYPACT:** Maine participates, so psychologists with PSYPACT authority can practice telepsychology with clients located there.\n- **Social Work Licensure Compact:** Maine has enacted it, but the compact isn't issuing multistate licenses yet.\n\nCompact status changes often. See [Counseling Compact, PSYPACT, and the Social Work Compact](/resources/for-therapists/counseling-compact-psypact) and the [Counseling Compact map](https://counselingcompact.org/map/compact-states/).\n\n## What VA care is available in Maine?\n\nVA medical centers serving Maine include facilities in Togus, near Augusta. Use [VA's facility locator](https://www.va.gov/find-locations/) for clinics and Vet Centers near a client.\n\nMaine is in Community Care Network Region 1, run by Optum. VA has started moving to new network contracts, so regions and administrators may change. Maine is one of the most rural states in the country, and many Veterans live hours from Togus.\n\n## How does ValorWell work for therapists in Maine?\n\nValorWell is telehealth-first. You work from wherever you are, as a 1099 contractor:\n\n- You make the clinical decisions and set your availability and capacity.\n- ValorWell handles credentialing, authorizations, billing, and claims for CHAMPVA, VA Community Care, and the ValorWell Foundation.\n- You're paid weekly for sessions you documented, and denials don't come out of your pay.\n- The arrangement is nonexclusive, so you can keep a private practice too.\n\nFor the full picture, see [How ValorWell Works for Therapists](/resources/for-therapists/valorwell-model-for-therapists) and [What a Therapist Needs to Join ValorWell](/resources/for-therapists/therapist-requirements-valorwell).\n\n## Important limits\n\n- **Need isn't a referral guarantee.** Volume depends on client eligibility, authorizations, and fit.\n- **Fully licensed only.** Associates and prescribers aren't a fit right now.\n- **Check the board.** License titles and rules can change; the state board is the authority.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, if you hold a Maine license or a valid compact privilege. What matters is where the client is located during the session.",
        "question": "Can I see ValorWell clients in Maine if I live in another state?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes. ValorWell accepts the independent LCPC license, along with LMFTs, independently licensed clinical social workers, and psychologists.",
        "question": "Does ValorWell accept LCPCs in Maine?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Community Care Network Region 1, run by Optum, under VA's current contracts.",
        "question": "Which VA network region is Maine in?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Veterans, Veteran spouses, and children of Veterans, covered through CHAMPVA, VA Community Care, or the ValorWell Foundation. You set the youngest age you'll see.",
        "question": "Who are the clients in Maine?"
      }
    ],
