    "summary": "ValorWell needs licensed therapists in Tennessee to treat Veterans and their families by telehealth. Licenses, compacts, VA care, and how it works.",
    "body_markdown": "## Is ValorWell hiring therapists in Tennessee?\n\nYes. ValorWell has a great need for more licensed therapists in Tennessee. Veterans, Veteran spouses, and children of Veterans there are looking for therapists who accept CHAMPVA and VA Community Care, and there aren't enough.\n\nVA estimates about 425,756 Veterans live in Tennessee, according to VA's [fiscal year 2025 Annual Benefits Report](https://benefits.va.gov/REPORTS/abr/docs/2025-abr.pdf).\n\n## Which licenses can treat Veterans and families in Tennessee?\n\nThe independent counselor license in Tennessee is the **LPC-MHSP** (Licensed Professional Counselor with Mental Health Service Provider designation), issued by the [Tennessee Board for Licensed Professional Counselors, Licensed Marital and Family Therapists, and Licensed Clinical Pastoral Therapists](https://www.tn.gov/health/licensure/pct.html). Tennessee also licenses LPCs; the MHSP designation is needed to diagnose and treat independently. ValorWell works with the independent clinical license. Licensed marriage and family therapists, independently licensed clinical social workers, and licensed psychologists in Tennessee also qualify, under the titles Tennessee uses.\n\nFor telehealth, the license has to match where the client is sitting during the session. To see a client located in Tennessee, you need a Tennessee license or a valid compact privilege. See [Can Therapists See Telehealth Clients in Another State?](/resources/for-therapists/telehealth-licensure-client-location)\n\n## Can you practice in Tennessee through a compact?\n\n- **Counseling Compact:** Tennessee is a member state and is issuing privileges to practice, so counselors whose home state is also an active member can apply for a privilege to practice in Tennessee.\n- **PSYPACT:** Tennessee participates, so psychologists with PSYPACT authority can practice telepsychology with clients located there.\n- **Social Work Licensure Compact:** Tennessee has enacted it, but the compact isn't issuing multistate licenses yet.\n\nCompact status changes often. See [Counseling Compact, PSYPACT, and the Social Work Compact](/resources/for-therapists/counseling-compact-psypact) and the [Counseling Compact map](https://counselingcompact.org/map/compact-states/).\n\n## What VA care is available in Tennessee?\n\nVA medical centers serving Tennessee include facilities in Memphis, Nashville, Murfreesboro, and Mountain Home. Use [VA's facility locator](https://www.va.gov/find-locations/) for clinics and Vet Centers near a client.\n\nTennessee is in Community Care Network Region 3, run by Optum. VA has started moving to new network contracts, so regions and administrators may change. Tennessee began issuing Counseling Compact privileges in September 2026.\n\n## How does ValorWell work for therapists in Tennessee?\n\nValorWell is telehealth-first. You work from wherever you are, as a 1099 contractor:\n\n- You make the clinical decisions and set your availability and capacity.\n- ValorWell handles credentialing, authorizations, billing, and claims for CHAMPVA, VA Community Care, and the ValorWell Foundation.\n- You're paid weekly for sessions you documented, and denials don't come out of your pay.\n- The arrangement is nonexclusive, so you can keep a private practice too.\n\nFor the full picture, see [How ValorWell Works for Therapists](/resources/for-therapists/valorwell-model-for-therapists) and [What a Therapist Needs to Join ValorWell](/resources/for-therapists/therapist-requirements-valorwell).\n\n## Important limits\n\n- **Need isn't a referral guarantee.** Volume depends on client eligibility, authorizations, and fit.\n- **Fully licensed only.** Associates and prescribers aren't a fit right now.\n- **Check the board.** License titles and rules can change; the state board is the authority.",
    "faq": [
      {
        "answer": "Yes, if you hold a Tennessee license or a valid compact privilege. What matters is where the client is located during the session.",
        "question": "Can I see ValorWell clients in Tennessee if I live in another state?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes. ValorWell accepts the independent LPC-MHSP license, along with LMFTs, independently licensed clinical social workers, and psychologists.",
        "question": "Does ValorWell accept LPC-MHSPs in Tennessee?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Community Care Network Region 3, run by Optum, under VA's current contracts.",
        "question": "Which VA network region is Tennessee in?"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Veterans, Veteran spouses, and children of Veterans, covered through CHAMPVA, VA Community Care, or the ValorWell Foundation. You set the youngest age you'll see.",
        "question": "Who are the clients in Tennessee?"
      }
    ],
