    "public_updated_at": "2026-10-14T18:43:54.610011+00:00",
    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "for-therapists",
    "sort_order": 2,
    "quick_answer": "Yes. Private practice and many contractor arrangements let you choose your capacity with no minimum. Most W-2 agency and group jobs set a minimum because salaries and overhead depend on volume. Without a minimum, you gain control but your income depends on the sessions you actually hold.",
