    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "champva",
    "sort_order": 3,
    "quick_answer": "Most CHAMPVA care doesn't need approval first. The exceptions are non-emergency inpatient mental health and substance use care, residential treatment, partial hospitalization, intensive outpatient programs, ABA treatment, covered dental care, and organ or bone marrow transplants. If your other insurance already approved the care, or it's through CITI at a VA facility, CHAMPVA doesn't need its own approval.",
