    "resource_kind": "article",
    "category_slug": "for-therapists",
    "sort_order": 7,
    "quick_answer": "The reasons are consistent: rigid schedules, productivity quotas, heavy documentation, high caseloads, limited say in clinical decisions, and pay that doesn't match the workload. Not every agency job is like that, and many offer real benefits, but those pressures push many clinicians toward private practice or contract work.",
